# Normalise line endings in the repository, not in each contributor's checkout.
#
# Without this file, `core.autocrlf=true` (the Windows Git default) checks the
# tree out with CRLF while .editorconfig declares `end_of_line = lf`. Prettier
# honours .editorconfig, so `npm run format:check` then fails on every single
# file on Windows even though the content is correct. Declaring the policy here
# makes the working tree identical on every platform.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Shell scripts must keep LF or they break under sh with a confusing error.
*.sh text eol=lf
Makefile text eol=lf

# Binary assets must never be line-ending translated.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.docx binary
*.xlsx binary
*.pdf binary
